./LOGBOOK.md:9:- IMPLEMENTATION: The selected libssh2 path now consumes one immutable snapshot-backed `SSHApprovedHostIdentityPolicy`. It accepts only an exact reviewed algorithm plus SHA-256 fingerprint tuple, validates the raw SSH wire key shape, binds the canonical host and port, checks revoked before approved records, and returns typed first-use, changed, revoked, unsupported, host-mismatch, or malformed outcomes before credential lookup.
./LOGBOOK.md:10:- PRIVACY AND ROTATION: Raw host-key bytes remain inside pre-auth policy input and no longer enter accepted session or credential values. First use returns bounded algorithm/fingerprint/canonical-host evidence for an explicit containing-app action; approved/revoked matches return only provenance and first/previous-last/observed timestamps. Printable evidence, decisions, inputs, and acceptance redact host, fingerprint, timestamps, and raw bytes.
./LOGBOOK.md:12:- VERIFICATION: Focused Swift Testing covers first use, same/different key, invalid label with identical bytes, malformed key, sequential rotation generations, one-active-approval validation, revocation, canonical-host/port mismatch, unsupported precedence, production composition, and redaction. A loopback libssh2 test proves all untrusted/rejected outcomes keep credential-provider calls, authentication attempts, and destination channels at zero.
./LOGBOOK.md:13:- VALIDATION: The corrected loader (13 tests), host-policy (9 tests), and live libssh2 ordering (1 test) regressions pass, as do strict recursive format lint and `swift build`. `make validate-core` first returned 0 with boundaries, native/libssh2 verification, all 413 Swift tests, and build passing. After a test-only expansion of malformed ordering coverage, a second full run passed every host-policy test but hung for more than four minutes in the untouched real-HEV 100-cycle test and was interrupted with exit 130; the final focused suites, lint, diff check, and build returned 0. No HEV code was changed.
./LOGBOOK.md:15:### 1838 — macOS provider resolves exact system-domain Keychain credentials (TASK-260715-1o9wjz)
./LOGBOOK.md:16:- IMPLEMENTATION: The macOS provider now resolves the file-based system-domain Keychain with `SecKeychainCopyDomainDefault(.system, ...)` and performs one read-only generic-password lookup using an explicit one-Keychain `kSecMatchSearchList`, fixed non-identifying service, exact canonical credential reference, `kSecUseDataProtectionKeychain=false`, and match limit one. The query surface has no hard-coded Keychain path, ambient search, enumeration, fallback, add/update/delete operation, access group, or accessibility attribute.
./LOGBOOK.md:17:- FORMAT AND PRIVACY: The strict `CredentialRecordV1` decoder enforces magic/version, exact reference and generation, bounds, trailing-byte rejection, optional-passphrase state, and constant-time digest comparison before an injected format registry constructs the external signer. Stable redacted errors distinguish not-provisioned, access-denied, wrong-class, generation, malformed, passphrase, unsupported-key, and cancellation outcomes. The accepted downstream key-format owner has not assigned production format IDs, so the default registry deliberately fails closed while imported/generated fixture registries exercise the candidate-neutral libssh2 seam.
./LOGBOOK.md:18:- LIFETIME: Mutable record/key/passphrase/digest buffers are cleared best-effort in bounded scopes, Security-call cancellation discards and clears returned data, and libssh2 retires the parsed credential after authentication or cancellation. Immutable Swift, Security-framework, allocator, and parser copies remain outside any provable zeroization guarantee.
./LOGBOOK.md:19:- VERIFICATION: Eleven focused resolver tests include a real two-throwaway-Keychain positive/negative search-list boundary with placeholder-only bytes; 56 combined resolver/SSH/provider tests and the complete 403-test/33-suite run pass. `make validate-core`, recursive Swift format lint, core boundaries, static forbidden-surface scan, build, and diff checks all exit 0. The required deprecated file-based `SecKeychain` API emits SDK deprecation warnings but is the accepted daemon/system-domain mechanism.
./LOGBOOK.md:22:### 1736 — macOS provider captures one complete non-secret SSH profile generation (TASK-260715-3f4lxy)
./LOGBOOK.md:23:- IMPLEMENTATION: `SSHProfileSnapshotV1` now carries the accepted complete profile, canonical endpoint, credential reference/generation, ordered host-key policy, and trust history as immutable value types. A strict deterministic JSON pass enforces UTF-8, sorted keys, canonical strings/numbers, no insignificant whitespace, duplicate rejection, depth 8, exact v1 envelope headers, recursive prohibited-field names, and exhaustive field invariants before exposing the model.
./LOGBOOK.md:24:- DECISION: The 4096-byte bound is checked over the actual binary-property-list representation of the exact three-key `providerConfiguration`, so owner and manager-contract metadata count toward the NetworkExtension envelope. The macOS adapter reads only `NETunnelProviderProtocol.providerConfiguration`; it has no App Group, Keychain, route, network, packet, or profile-write path.
./LOGBOOK.md:25:- GENERATION SAFETY: A fresh `SSHProfileRuntimeSnapshotLoader` owns one runtime start. A present exact five-field v1 start request binds `configurationGeneration` to the SHA-256 digest of the exact stored canonical snapshot bytes before first capture; nil options may capture the validated stored value. Byte-identical rereads return the original capture, while stale requests, same-generation field replacement, newer-generation replacement, and concurrent competing captures fail with the fixed privacy-safe `profileGenerationMismatch` error.
./LOGBOOK.md:36:- ROOT CAUSE: `neagent` previously received zero PlugInKit matches because both the development-signed host and embedded packet-tunnel provider omitted `com.apple.security.app-sandbox`. Adding App Sandbox to both exact targets made PlugInKit discover one provider at the expected embedded path after launch; Network Extension stayed exactly `packet-tunnel-provider`, with no App Groups or signed Keychain Sharing entitlement.
./LOGBOOK.md:37:- PHYSICAL RESULT: On the designated arm64 Mac15,9 running macOS 26.5/Xcode 26.5, the rebuilt archive passed 49 inside-out inspection assertions and nine negative drift cases. Ten start/message/stop cycles plus host termination exited 0 with one manager and no provider process; exact-path user-Applications uninstall/reinstall, PlugInKit rediscovery, and a final cycle also exited 0. No probe crash report or privacy finding was present.
./LOGBOOK.md:39:- UNRELATED REGRESSION CHECK: An extra full `swift test` run built but exited 1 with 377/378 passing when `HEVUDPDatagramAdapterTests/nonterminalRelayErrorsPreserveAssociation` transiently observed zero active associations; the exact test immediately passed alone. A full retry later stopped emitting output and was cancelled after roughly two minutes (exit 130, one cancellation handler pending). This code is outside the probe rework and no aggregate-suite pass is claimed; all task-scoped gates exit 0.
./LOGBOOK.md:42:- PASS: On the designated arm64 Mac15,9 running macOS 26.5/Xcode 26.5, the accepted archive passed all 47 nested signature, designated-requirement, profile, entitlement, architecture, and privacy assertions. Four contract tests pass with 91.80% line coverage for `ProbeContract.swift`; the new physical-runner parser/privacy tests and lint gates pass.
./LOGBOOK.md:44:- RESUME: An authorized person must accept the macOS VPN-configuration approval in the foreground probe window. Then rerun ten cycles, exact-path uninstall/reinstall, and the final cycle using the task-scoped redacted runbook. No Gate P0 pass is claimed before those physical checks succeed.
./LOGBOOK.md:47:- IMPLEMENTATION: A separate XcodeGen macOS 14 arm64 project now contains `works.relux.tunnel.probe.mac`, exactly one embedded `works.relux.tunnel.probe.mac.tunnel` app extension, a v1 JSON request/response contract, privacy-safe lifecycle/status reporting, and save/reload/enable/start/message/stop host paths. The provider installs no network settings, reads no packet flow, forwards no packets, and owns no worker tasks.
./LOGBOOK.md:48:- SIGNING: The initial background process could select the approved profile/identity but could not use the login-Keychain private key (`errSecInternalComponent`). Running the same checked-in command through the approved Aqua Terminal seam resolved that execution-context issue without exporting a key or weakening policy. Both profile-scoped signing preflights and the signed archive then passed.
./LOGBOOK.md:50:- SCOPE: `Package.swift`, existing `Sources/`, root `scripts/`, release workflows, and `Makefile` remain untouched. The archived product and privacy-safe inspection log are under `.temp/TASK-260715-1r0fxv/`; no secret signing material is recorded.
./LOGBOOK.md:57:- SCOPE EVIDENCE: Exactly four local provisioning profiles changed during the run and all four are the approved macOS development set; no unexpected, iOS, or distribution profile changed. The isolated harness declared no App Group, Keychain Sharing, iOS, distribution, or legacy-bundle mutation, and raw profiles/certificates were neither attached nor committed.
./LOGBOOK.md:64:- ACCESS ANOMALIES: Read-only Safari automation stalled and was terminated at exit 130 without page data. A named-profile `notarytool history` probe exited 1 because the default Keychain was locked; `TASK-260728-dveo1o` owns revalidation after unattended Keychain access is restored. No secret, credential, certificate private key, recovery code, or full device identifier was captured.
./LOGBOOK.md:72:- REVIEW VERDICT: BLOCKED. The privacy-safe record is honest, the r12 matrix and live-consumer gates pass, and the targeted leak scan is clean, but the record itself says the ceremony resumed across 2026-07-28 and 2026-08-10 with producer/reviewer work between interactions and without captured interaction start/end times. That directly fails literal AC1.
./LOGBOOK.md:74:- RESOLUTION: Recommended path is one newly timed, uninterrupted owner sitting that idempotently repeats/confirms every in-scope grant, captures privacy-safe contemporaneous facts, and runs with history/echo suppression. Alternative is an explicit owner architecture/product decision to amend AC1/AC2/AC3/AC7 and ADR-028 to accept resumed functional evidence; accepting the current record under the unchanged contract is not valid.
