./LOGBOOK.md:101:- ROOT CAUSE: A reserved timeout race resumed teardown after its first child resolved but remained registered until both children retired. Teardown exposed completion without draining that registry, and it did not arrange durable automatic-task retirement until after socket close; if a cancellation-ignoring socket consumed the close deadline, the join branch was skipped and completed automatic-task references remained permanently counted.
./LOGBOOK.md:102:- REWORK: Automatic-task retirement now starts before socket close and clears actor-owned references only after every cancelled task actually returns. The reserved registry is drained within the existing close deadline, so cooperative races reconcile before completion while genuinely non-cooperative socket work remains visible until its safe late return.
