./LOGBOOK.md:144:### 1758 — libssh2 adapter loopback conformance closes review round 2 (TASK-260715-1ozsb6)
./LOGBOOK.md:145:- ROOT CAUSE: libssh2 keeps channel-open and reply-requiring global-request nonblocking state on the shared session, so actor reentrancy across `EAGAIN` allowed a second open to resume the first open's state. The custom send/receive callback ABI also requires negative socket errors directly; returning `-1` plus `errno=EAGAIN` made ordinary backpressure appear as a disconnect.
