./LOGBOOK.md:541:### 1630 — Relay UDP I/O uses readiness-only retry and bounded resolver inspection (TASK-260715-3xpc6b)
./LOGBOOK.md:542:- IMPLEMENTATION: Registry-owned nonblocking IPv4/IPv6 sockets now perform one `sendto` attempt per client datagram and bounded `recvmsg` turns. Replies preserve the kernel-observed source family, address, port, and payload bytes. `EAGAIN` returns a readiness-only retry result without idle activity or an internal retry buffer; `ENOBUFS`, oversize/truncation, terminal socket errors, closed/stale associations, and sink pressure map to finite wire errors or documented counted drops.
