./LOGBOOK.md:981:### 0908 — Review: minimal ReluxNIOSSH fork accepted; two adapter-facing caveats (TASK-260715-nzdzv3)
./LOGBOOK.md:982:- MILESTONE: Fork accepted → `done`. Reviewer independently re-ran every gate: `make validate-reluxniossh` (exact archive/license SHA-256, 16-file allowlist, 323 upstream XCTest + 10 Swift Testing, build), strict `swift format lint`, same-pin `conflict-test`, `make validate-core` (49 tests/build) — all exit 0. Default-path equivalence of the new adjust math to upstream verified analytically for even window sizes (default 1<<24); protected-byte boundary matches contract §10.1 (post-encode pre-write at `NIOSSHHandler.swift:266`, post-read pre-decode at `NIOSSHHandler.swift:205`); all outbound frames flow through the single `writeMessage` path.
./LOGBOOK.md:983:- FINDING: During any KEX (client- or server-initiated) upstream's state machine rejects outbound `channelData` with `protocolViolation` (`SSHConnectionStateMachine.swift:1060-1076`), failing the child write promise. Pre-existing upstream behavior, unchanged by the fork — but automatic byte/time rekey makes the collision window likely under bulk traffic. The NIOSSH adapter (TASK-260715-1af33i) MUST gate/queue child writes on `rekeySnapshot.keyExchangeInProgress` / `NIOSSHRekeyStartedEvent`→`NIOSSHRekeySucceededEvent`; the fork exposes exactly this observability for the contract's "writes MAY suspend" clause.
./LOGBOOK.md:984:- FINDING: `NIOSSHChannelWindowConfiguration` invariant is `remaining + buffered + delivered == initialWindowSize`, so remaining credit never grows past `initialWindowSize` even when `maximumWindowSize` is larger, and a `windowAdjustmentThreshold > initialWindowSize` (allowed by preconditions, which only check ≤ max) permanently withholds WINDOW_ADJUST — a stalled-channel footgun. Adapter policy must keep threshold ≤ initial (≤ half is sane). Cap semantics remain contract-correct: `remainingBefore + adjustment ≤ cap` always holds.
./LOGBOOK.md:987:### 0850 — Minimal ReluxNIOSSH window/rekey fork is reviewable (TASK-260715-nzdzv3)
./LOGBOOK.md:988:- DECISION: The source fork is an independent SwiftPM package at `Dependencies/ReluxNIOSSH`, based byte-for-byte on SwiftNIO SSH `0.14.1` / `31cdc3c` before a 16-file allowlisted delta. The `NIOSSH` product/module and upstream 16 MiB/no-auto-rekey defaults remain source-compatible; `ReluxTunnelCore` has no dependency on the fork.
./LOGBOOK.md:992:### 0821 — Candidate-neutral SSH conformance contract closes the shared-surface gap (TASK-260715-2ny6z4)
./LOGBOOK.md:993:- DECISION: Both engine adapters use one serialized, type-erased `ReluxTunnelCore` boundary with mandatory raw host-key policy evaluation before credential access, bounded partial writes, independent byte-stream halves, capped observable per-channel receive credit, automatic byte/time plus explicit/server rekey, keepalive, stable errors, schema-v1 metrics/events, and privacy-safe opaque lane identity. ADR-014 remains open; unsupported mandatory behavior is a red matrix row, never a candidate-specific skip.
./LOGBOOK.md:994:- FINDING: The existing `SSHContracts.swift` is intentionally only an M0 boundary skeleton and no board item owned implementation of the reviewed semantic surface before both adapters and the common suite. Created atomic TASK-260720-100wu6 and linked it between this contract and TASK-260715-1af33i, TASK-260715-1ozsb6, and TASK-260715-2d3g5e; the independent NIOSSH fork continues to consume this contract directly.
./LOGBOOK.md:995:- VERIFICATION: The contract defines every operation, state, timeout/cancellation scope, error, metric, privacy rule, and E-ALGO/E-HOSTAUTH/E-CHANNELS/E-BACKPRESSURE/E-WINDOW/E-REKEY/E-KEEPALIVE/E-CANCEL/E-SCALE/E-ERRORS/E-METRICS-PRIVACY/E-INJECTION row. Three task-scoped PlantUML sources pass syntax checking and their lifecycle, pre-auth host verification, and channel/window/rekey SVG renders were visually inspected.
