./LOGBOOK.md:1002:### 0759 — SSH engine source audit pins fixed baselines without selecting an engine (TASK-260715-28ok1k)
./LOGBOOK.md:1003:- SECURITY: SwiftNIO SSH is pinned to `0.14.1` / `31cdc3c`, which fixes critical CVE-2026-43798, with resolved Swift Crypto `4.5.1` and SwiftNIO `2.101.3` security-patched transitives. libssh2 release `1.11.1` is not a clean baseline because six advisories were fixed after release; the candidate is pinned to untagged `1.11.2_DEV` commit `a343024` containing all six fixes, with OpenSSL `3.5.7`. Re-audit on a signed libssh2 1.11.2+ release is mandatory.
./LOGBOOK.md:1004:- FINDING: SwiftNIO SSH hardcodes each child receive-window target to 16 MiB and exposes client `_rekey()` only internally. libssh2 exposes generic per-channel initial/remaining/adjust APIs, but its direct-tcpip helper fixes the 2 MiB default and it likewise has no public client-rekey API or automatic byte/time threshold.
./LOGBOOK.md:1005:- DECISION: ADR-014 remains open. Both candidates retain identical host-key, window, sustained 5 GiB rekey, scale (through 1,000 channels), cancellation, algorithm, extension-build, memory, and physical-size gates. Unknowns are named experiments in `.research/260720_task-260715-28ok1k-ssh-engine-candidate-audit.md`; no missing capability was waived.
./LOGBOOK.md:1006:- RISK: libssh2 master issue #2023 contains an unresolved AEAD correctness report whose specific leak interpretation is disputed. Treat it as an ASan/packet-content experiment, not a proven leak or a reason to prejudge the engine.
