./Dependencies/ReluxNIOSSH/Sources/NIOSSH/NIOSSHError.swift:15:/// An error thrown by NIOSSH.
./Dependencies/ReluxNIOSSH/Sources/NIOSSH/NIOSSHError.swift:17:/// For extensibility purposes, ``NIOSSHError``s are composed of two parts. The first part is an
./Dependencies/ReluxNIOSSH/Sources/NIOSSH/NIOSSHError.swift:19:/// The second part is some opaque diagnostic data. This is not visible to your code, but is used to
./Dependencies/ReluxNIOSSH/Sources/NIOSSH/NIOSSHError.swift:20:/// help provide extra information for diagnostic purposes when logging this error.
./Dependencies/ReluxNIOSSH/Sources/NIOSSH/NIOSSHError.swift:22:/// Note that due to this construction ``NIOSSHError`` is not equatable: only the ``NIOSSHError/type`` is. This is deliberate,
./Dependencies/ReluxNIOSSH/Sources/NIOSSH/NIOSSHError.swift:23:/// as it is possible two errors have the same type but a different underlying cause or diagnostic data. For
./Dependencies/ReluxNIOSSH/Sources/NIOSSH/NIOSSHError.swift:24:/// this reason, if you need to compare two ``NIOSSHError`` values you should explicitly compare their ``NIOSSHError/type``.
