     }
     #expect(started.duration(to: .now) < .seconds(1))
     #expect((await transport.snapshot()).connectionState == .closed)

codex
A mapping audit found one important edge case before the broad run: a transport timeout during credential lookup or authentication could inherit an authentication label. I’m tightening the precedence so timeout/cancellation/transient transport interruption are classified before security stages, preserving the requirement that operational failures never masquerade as trust or authentication rejection.
